  "summary": "The treiber stack implementation in heapless had a race condition",
  "details": "In the affected versions, it was possible for two threads or execution contexts running concurrently to race, causing one to read out of a pointer that had been invalidated by another execution context.\n\nReported by [Jacob Finkelman](https://github.com/Eh2406).",
